IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nsa-symbols`

-- National Symbols Act 2022, ss 3 to 15, 17, 19 and the Schedules -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_national-symbols-act-2022.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `ss 3 to 12 -- the symbols declared`

#ASSERT `the category of` `the National Flag` EQUALS `a national symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the National Anthem` EQUALS `a national symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the National Pledge` EQUALS `a national symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the National Coat of Arms` EQUALS `a national symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the public seal` EQUALS `a national symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the Lion Head symbol` EQUALS `a national symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the national flower` EQUALS `a national symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the Presidential Standard` EQUALS `a presidential symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the Presidential Coat of Arms` EQUALS `a presidential symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the seal of the President` EQUALS `a presidential symbol`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the Merlion` EQUALS `not a symbol under this Act`
#ASSERT `the category of` `the flag of another state` EQUALS `not a symbol under this Act`

#ASSERT `the declaring section` `the National Flag` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the declaring section` `the Lion Head symbol` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the declaring section` `the seal of the President` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the declaring section` `the Merlion` EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `is a symbol under this Act` `the Lion Head symbol`
#ASSERT NOT `is a symbol under this Act` `the Merlion`

#ASSERT `the number of languages the Pledge is set out in` EQUALS 4

§ `ss 7(3), 12(3) -- custody of the seals`

#ASSERT `is to be kept by the President` `the public seal`
#ASSERT `is to be kept by the President` `the seal of the President`
#ASSERT NOT `is to be kept by the President` `the National Flag`

§ `First Schedule Part 1 -- the flag's design`

#ASSERT `matches the National Flag description` red white TRUE 5 60 90
#ASSERT `matches the National Flag description` red white TRUE 5 100 150
#ASSERT NOT `matches the National Flag description` red white TRUE 5 60 120
#ASSERT NOT `matches the National Flag description` red white TRUE 4 60 90
#ASSERT NOT `matches the National Flag description` white red TRUE 5 60 90
#ASSERT NOT `matches the National Flag description` red white FALSE 5 60 90

§ `First Schedule Part 7 -- the national flower`

#ASSERT `is the national flower` `Vanda Miss Joaquim`
#ASSERT `is the national flower` `Papilionanthe Miss Joaquim`
#ASSERT NOT `is the national flower` `Bougainvillea`

§ `ss 13, 14(1) -- who decides`

#ASSERT `may amend the Schedules` `the President` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `may amend the Schedules` `the Minister` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `may amend the Schedules` `the President` FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `may make regulations under this Act` `the President`
#ASSERT NOT `may make regulations under this Act` `the Minister`

§ `ss 14(2), 15 -- offences and prosecution`

#ASSERT `the regulation penalty is within s 14(2)(d)` 30000 6
#ASSERT NOT `the regulation penalty is within s 14(2)(d)` 30001 0
#ASSERT NOT `the regulation penalty is within s 14(2)(d)` 0 7

#ASSERT `the use can be an offence` `the National Flag` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the use can be an offence` `the National Flag` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the use can be an offence` `the National Flag` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the use can be an offence` `the Merlion` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `the prosecution may be instituted` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the prosecution may be instituted` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the prosecution may be instituted` FALSE FALSE

§ `ss 17, 19 -- the consequential amendments`

#ASSERT `is named in Evidence Act s 59(1)(f)` `the public seal`
#ASSERT `is named in Evidence Act s 59(1)(f)` `the seal of the President`
#ASSERT NOT `is named in Evidence Act s 59(1)(f)` `the National Coat of Arms`

#ASSERT `is a foreign national emblem` `the flag of another state`
#ASSERT NOT `is a foreign national emblem` `the National Flag`

